br("pulls old metal wick tabs and bits of debris out of chunks of leftover wax","Pull out the old wick tabs now. Fishing them out of hot liquid wax later is miserable.")

# ===== TOPIC 3: MELTING & COMBINING SAFELY =====
th("Now the fun part. Melting it all down. But please, do this safely.","kitchen")
full("a large metal pot of wax melting gently inside a bigger pot of simmering water","Never melt wax in a bare pan on direct heat. Always use a water bath, like this.","close-up")
split("Wax is flammable. A double boiler keeps it gentle and stops it from ever catching fire.","a double-boiler setup with a wax pot sitting inside a pot of simmering water","kitchen","left")
live("chunks of coloured wax slowly melting and merging into a pool of liquid in a pot","the solid chunks soften and slowly melt down into a smooth swirling liquid","The old wax melts down fast. Watch all those different candles turn into one pool of liquid.")
split("Use a thermometer. You want it fully melted, but never smoking. Smoking wax is dangerous.","a candy thermometer clipped to a pot of melted wax showing a safe temperature","kitchen","right")
full("leftover wicks and burnt debris being strained out of melted wax through a fine sieve","Strain it as you go. Old candles hide burnt wicks and grit you really do not want in there.","close-up")
live("several pots of melted wax being combined into one very large container","the streams of liquid wax merge and swirl together into one big golden pool","Then pour the batches together slowly. This is where twenty candles become one giant one.")
full("one big container of smooth combined melted wax, clean and golden","One big, clean pool of mixed wax. No debris, no old wicks, just liquid ready to pour.","close-up")
th("Work in batches if you have to. A giant candle takes a surprising amount of wax.")

# ===== TOPIC 4: FIXING THE SCENT =====
