split("Lean into one scent family. If your wax is warm and sweet, add a little vanilla.","a small bottle of vanilla fragrance oil being added to a pot of melted wax","kitchen","left")
full("a few amber fragrance oil bottles beside a pot of wax with a couple of drops going in","A few drops of one strong unifying scent pulls all those random smells into something intentional.","close-up")
full("a simple diagram-style shot of warm, fresh and woody scent groups kept separate","Warm with warm, fresh with fresh. Keep the families apart and the blend always works.","close-up")
th("If it smells muddy, do not panic. A neutral wax plus one bold scent always saves it.")
br("waves a hand over a pot of melted wax, leans in to smell it, then nods happily","I kept smelling mine as I went. When it smelled like one candle, not twenty, I stopped.")
